  "decisionReason": "The smooth-90 change is source-authoritative rather than fitted and produces a large, coherent improvement in both displacement and source-end-action fields, especially L20. On the clean frozen baseline it more than halves L19 source-action RMS error and reduces L20 restraint failures 5 -> 1 and source-action failures 137 -> 31. It therefore qualifies as a required B31J bend-mechanics correction for this all-90-degree Version-14/B31J-2017 benchmark. It is not a complete system solution: clean L19 still has node20090 FY and node21470 FY above 10%. The historical I015 composition demonstrates strong interaction but is retained only as secondary evidence; it does not restore transverse shear as the roadmap. The next step is prescribed source-component endpoint replay at CAESAR DOFs to isolate the remaining local formulation/load defects without global redistribution.",
